      "id": "claim_677ada1ad8954e7ab10c0fb91630d38d",
      "statement": "NEPO uses Drizzle ORM over the postgres.js driver against PostgreSQL: backend/src/db/index.ts creates the client from config.databaseUrl and exports db = drizzle(client, { schema }) from a single ~1300-line schema file backend/src/db/schema.ts. Migrations live under backend/drizzle/ (one NNNN_name.sql per migration plus meta/ holding the drizzle-kit journal and snapshots) — there is no backend/src/db/migrations directory. All status/type columns use pgEnum declarations at the top of schema.ts (lines 23-48; salary_confirmation_status is declared beside its table at line 620), covering trip_status, fuel_mode, loading_type, role, txn_type, trailer_type, truck/trailer/driver/customer status, penalty_status, vehicle_component, vehicle_schedule kind/status, advance_request/settlement status, notification_type, work_day_status, and salary_confirmation_status.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/drizzle.config.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:b03cdf885464bef6d10a7e5aa72100fb33ee5e09714da0c64bdf7bae3a472e69"
