    {
      "id": "claim_fc58fdd1581e41e89e534057dededc15",
      "statement": "The ledger table (schema.ts:405) implements the project's loosely-coupled entity reference convention: entityType is a varchar(50) string — narrowed by the service layer to CUSTOMER | DRIVER | VENDOR | FORWARDER | CARRIER (external carriers live in customers, vendors in suppliers) — and entityId is an integer, both deliberately without foreign keys so the ledger outlives the entity. balance is numeric(15, 0) for exact VND precision. The same polymorphic pattern appears in billing_documents.entityType/entityId and expenses.truckId + vehicle_component, where integrity is maintained by service paths because Postgres cannot enforce a polymorphic FK.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/src/db/schema.ts#L405-L426",
