    {
      "id": "claim_361a3516b9484fbbbef11e1d7d3c8d0d",
      "statement": "pgvector support exists only through a Drizzle customType: schema.ts declares vectorColumn1536 whose SQL type is vector(1536) (JS representation is the pgvector literal '[0.1,0.2,...]'). It types faq_entries.embedding and knowledge_chunks.embedding, and because the type is opaque to Drizzle all vector reads and writes go through raw SQL (faq-fast-lane.ts cosine queries with <=>, backfill-faq-embeddings.ts UPDATE ... ::vector). Migration 0104_faq_knowledge_base.sql runs CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector and creates the partial HNSW cosine index (WHERE embedding IS NOT NULL AND is_active = TRUE); 0107 repeats the pattern for knowledge_chunks. Both dev (docker-compose.dev.yml) and prod (deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml) therefore run the pgvector/pgvector:pg16 image — upstream postgres:16 plus the extension — because stock postgres:16-alpine lacks it.",
