    {
      "id": "claim_45331efb739f4404b7c6b3831163f54e",
      "statement": "Migration numbering in backend/drizzle/ has deliberate collisions and gaps — several numbers carry two distinct forward migrations (0050, 0051, 0062, 0079, 0104, 0106), some pair a migration with a same-numbered *.revert.sql rollback file (0048 through 0053), and numbers like 0060 and 0089-0093 are skipped (the journal jumps 0088 to 0094). Never renumber by hand: make prod-migrate applies files in lexicographic filename order and drizzle-kit migrate follows the journal, and both orderings already account for the existing names. Applying SQL manually also desyncs drizzle-kit's snapshot — 0104_parallel_guardian.sql records that a duplicate CREATE TABLE faq_entries had to be stripped from a generated migration for exactly this reason.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Makefile#L180-L198",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:efbe9112f20b583bf250b892bbf52397a1bf28c4c8986674a8698cb58c628527:"
