    {
      "id": "claim_56a8358b5acc4800a72621758b3d78c8",
      "statement": "deletedAt soft delete is the default convention: most business tables carry a nullable deleted_at, queries filter deletedAt IS NULL, and uniqueness under soft delete uses partial unique indexes (e.g. customers_active_name_tax_code_uniq_idx applies WHERE deleted_at IS NULL). Tires are the deliberate exception: migration 0084_hard_delete_tires.sql purges soft-deleted tire rows and the /fleet/tires CRUD router passes deleteMode: 'hard', so user cleanup frees the unique serial number while business history is carried by status DISPOSED. Append-only/infra tables (ledger, audit_logs, agent_*) have no soft delete by design.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/drizzle/0084_hard_delete_tires.sql",
