    {
      "id": "claim_8cd779fa7ea34c58b386c3e5cb1a8788",
      "statement": "Migration 0117_fuel_allocation_unit_price_multi_row.sql enables multi-row fuel purchases per trip: it drops the trip_fuel_allocations_supplier_once_idx and _cash_once_idx partial unique indexes (which had allowed one supplier purchase and one cash purchase per trip) and adds a nullable unit_price numeric(12,2). NULL means legacy/derive-at-read — the row is priced with the trip's effective price (fuelActualUnitPrice otherwise fuelPriceApplied) — while rows with an explicit unitPrice are priced at that price in ledger.service.ts. The table's CHECK constraints still hold per row: liters > 0, CREDIT rows must carry a supplierId, CASH rows must have none.",
